// control-h0-nodepth (t_96daf53b): half colour output, NO depth declared.
//
// A half colour output is the only thing that makes the reference set the
// container's outputFromH0 flag - measured 2026-09-06: half ARITHMETIC does
// not (the float twin compiled with the reference's fast-precision switch
// turns its whole body half and still writes its colour to the full-precision
// output with the flag clear), so the flag tracks the DECLARED OUTPUT TYPE and
// nothing else.  This shader and sd_h0_nodepth_twin.fcg differ in one source
// token and, in the container, in that flag plus the output instruction's
// register and precision bits: three bytes of 208, measured.
//
// WHAT THIS ROW IS FOR.  The flag decides which control word the SDK binds
// (cell/gcm/gcm_fp_control.h, which carries the bit facts and their
// provenance - no value is repeated here, because those values have already
// moved once and a fixture that hard-codes them would have to be edited every
// time the runtime learns something).  Until 2026-09-06 the SDK bound a half
// output with the depth-export bit set, inherited from PSL1GHT, so a program
// declaring NO depth exported whatever its R1.z held.  This pair caught that,
// and it stays in the manifest to catch it coming back.
//
// It declares no depth on either side, so the judge cannot derive the question
// from the declarations - a BIND defect writes a surface the container never
// named.  The row therefore opts in with judge=z, and its expectation is
// IDENTICAL: the zeta must read the vertex program's own Z on both sides.
// A moved zeta here means the bind is exporting depth nobody asked for.
//
// registerCount is 2 and R1 is NEVER WRITTEN by this program, so a stray
// export reads a lane it never touched - deliberately, because this row's job
// is "did the bit fire at all" without depending on any model of what R1 holds.
// sd_h0_r1known.fcg is the companion that carries the number.  Both sides are
// reference-compiled: the variable under test is the bind, so a compiler
// difference would confound it.
void main(float4 t : TEXCOORD0, out half4 o : COLOR)
{
    o = t;
}
